Queue Reversal Difficulty: EasyAccuracy: 77.98%Submissions: 151K+Points: 2 Given a queue q containing integer elements, your task is to reverse the queue. Examples: Input: q[] = [5, 10, 15, 20, 25] Output: [25, 20, 15, 10, 5]


---------
class Solution {
public:
    void reverseQueue(queue<int> &q) {
        stack<int> st;
        while (!q.empty()) {
            st.push(q.front());
            q.pop();
        }
        while (!st.empty()) {
            q.push(st.top());
            st.pop();
        }
    }
};

--------


✅ Works because recursion goes till the last element, then pushes them back in reverse order.

Time Complexity: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(n) (due to recursion stack)
